        "The looms are so loud we talk with our lips. You learn to read them. Handy for gossip.",
        "The knocker-up taps on your window with a long pole at five. Who knocks him up? Nobody knows.",
        "Wakes week, the whole mill shuts and the town goes to the seaside. Same week. All of us.",
        "Clogs! Wooden soles, iron rims. Spark on the cobbles. Good for dancing, too.",
        "The brass band practises Tuesdays. The whole street knows the tunes by Thursday.",
        "My dad keeps racing pigeons on the roof. They always come home. Smarter than him, Mum says.",
        "The Mechanics Institute has evening classes. Work all day, learn all night. Then work again.",
