        "Pond dipping! Water boatmen, dragonfly nymphs, a newt if you're lucky. Put them back gently.",
        "We put tiny rings on the birds' legs. When someone finds one far away, we learn where it flew.",
        "The geese come in autumn. Thousands of them at dusk, all talking at once.",
        "A twitcher drove two hundred miles to see a bird. It flew off as he parked. He was very calm about it.",
