      folk: [
        "Rice grows standing in water. We plant every seedling by hand. My back knows every one.",
        "The water buffalo pulls the plough. She's slow, she's strong, and she has opinions.",
        "Ducks swim in the paddies and eat the bugs. Free help. Noisy, but free.",
        "The floating market starts before dawn. Boats piled with fruit, all bumping together.",
        "Lotus flowers grow out of the mud and come up perfectly clean. Like a good idea.",
        "Two harvests a year, sometimes three. The river brings the silt, the silt brings the rice.",
        "My hat is shaped like a cone so the rain runs off and the sun stays off. Best hat.",
        "The river spirit gets the first bowl of rice every harvest. We'd never forget.",
      ],
